urname><given-names>RM</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><source>The Demand for Food Away From Home: Full-Service or Fast Food?</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>Economic Research Service, USDA</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jabs</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Devine</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Time scarcity and food choices: An overview</article-title><source>Appetite</source><year>2006</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>196</fpage><lpage>204</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16698116</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jeffery</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>French</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Epidemic Obesity in the United States: Are Fast Foods and Television Viewing Contributing?</article-title><source>Am J Public Health</source><year>1998</year><volume>88</volume><fpage>277</fpage><lpage>280</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9491022</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thompson</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Ballew</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Resnicow</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Must</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Bandini</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Cyr</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Dietz</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Food purchased away from home as a predictor of change in BMI <italic>z</italic>-score among girls</article-title><source>International Journal of Obesity</source><year>2004</